   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1943-01-07">January 7. 1943</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__683" type="person">Mr. Lewis F. Gittler</rs><lb/>
               Office of War Information<lb/>
               224 West 57 Str.<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__683" type="person">Mr. Gittler</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I have received your <rs ref="#L10598" type="letter">letter of January 5th</rs>. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3339" type="person">My
               secretary</rs> has asked <rs ref="#" type="person">Mr.
                  Nathan</rs><!-- unklar wer gemeint ist, vielleicht Robert R. Nathan --> about a pay for my radio speech because
               <rs ref="tillich_person_id__1785" type="person">Mr. Siemsen</rs> was almost indignant when I doubted that I could ask for a
               renumeration. You will understand that I am not interested in losing two hours of my
               working time by registering $5- in order to receive $5 which may arrive after 2
               month.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Very sincerely yours</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"
                  >Paul Tillich</rs></signed><lb/>
               Professor at Union Theological Seminary. <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
